{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And HaShem will root them out from upon their land.</b> This section refers to the First Temple, for there they served idolatry, and He said, ״ויתשם — and He will root them out,״ and ״וישליכם — and He will cast them away,״ concerning the Ten Tribes, for from the day they were exiled they have not returned, and they are called נדחים (the banished/driven away). And from this He said, כיום הזה — 'like this day': that is, like this day, that you are gathered in the wilderness in one place but you are banished (נדחים), for you have not yet come to the rest and to the inheritance that you are destined to enter there — so too your children will be exiled to another land and will be gathered in one place, banished from their land." "<b>And cast them away to another land.</b> The ל״מד (lamed) of וישליכם is rabtati (large), and it is known that it is the largest of all the letters, and the reason it was made rabtati may be that it alludes to the great and exalted degree that is cast down in the time of exile — as Yirmeyah said (Lamentations 2:1): ״השליך משמים ארץ תפארת ישראל״, and so it is written further (Psalms 78:61): ״ותפארתו ביד צר״, and it is also written (Daniel 8:12): ״ותשלך אמת ארצה״ — and this is the icon of Ya'akov engraved upon the Throne of Glory. And this is what they said in the Midrash of Eikhah: 'Do they provoke Me except on account of the icon of Ya'akov engraved upon the Throne of Glory? This is what corrupts for their harm, as it is written: השליך משמים ארץ תפארת ישראל.' And this is what David, of blessed memory, said (Psalms 102:11): ״כי נשאתני ותשליכני״ — for the lofty and exalted degree was cast down; and once He cast down that degree, he did not remember the הדום רגליו (the footstool of His feet), which is the crown that receives from Tiferet, in the mystery of (Proverbs 4:9) ״עטרת תפארת תמגנך״, and this is what is written (Lamentations 5:16): ״נפלה עטרת ראשנו״, and once it fell, Yisra'el fell, as it is said (Amos 5:2): ״נפלה לא תוסיף קום בתולת ישראל״. And in this language we find that the prophet Yeḥezkel said concerning the kingdom of the house of David (Ezekiel 19:12): ״ותתש בחמה לארץ הושלכה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:05.859032782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}